# COVERAGE FIXTURE. Deliberate test data, not an ontology about anything.
#
# RULE: prp-inv2
# W3C OWL 2 Web Ontology Language Profiles (Second Edition), section 4.3,
# Table 5: The Semantics of Axioms about Properties.
# https://www.w3.org/TR/owl2-profiles/#Reasoning_in_OWL_2_RL_and_RDF_Graphs_using_Rules
#
#   T(?p1, owl:inverseOf, ?p2)
#   T(?x, ?p2, ?y)
#     ->  T(?y, ?p1, ?x)
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. The repository's own RDF never fires prp-inv2, so
# tools/horn_differential.py compared the Rust and Python engines on it zero
# times and its clean sweep said nothing about it.
#
# EXPECTED: exactly one derivation, credited to prp-inv2:
#   :y :p :x
#
# The mirror rule prp-inv1 then fires on that conclusion and re-derives
# ":x :q :y", which is already asserted, so it adds no step and takes no credit.

@prefix : <http://ex.org/cover/prp-inv2#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

:p owl:inverseOf :q .
:x :q :y .
